    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83774.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 36,
    "turn_text": "But, and of course, Sam Rayburn left no doubt he preferred the work horses, but I don't want to get too high in mind about that because, you know, there's something to being a show horse or at least to knowing that you really do have to Your good works don't speak for themselves. You really do have to reach out. You really do have to engage. And you have to think about how to make what you're doing engaging and exciting. That's fair enough. So I don't want to get totally absorbed in that messaging enterprise. But I also think that you know, the great yards are littered with members who thought they could be just work horses and think their good works would just be readily applauded even if they didn't do anything to let people know.",
