    "turn_text": "Listen, I watched the news like it's some, I did cut it off during COVID last year because I just couldn't, my blood pressure medicine wasn't strong enough, but I do watch it a lot. And in the 20 plus years that you've been my representative, I don't think I've ever seen you on a national news program. And I tell people all the time, I sort of like that. I mean, there are some who it seems live in the rotunda of the Capitol where the cameras are, and some whose names are never heard. You know, I, I, Marcy, Captain, and you come to mind as to who have been in Congress for a long time and have not necessarily sought praise or attention for it from a national audience. And I mean, I mean that as a compliment and a thank you as my representative. I appreciate that you're doing what you're doing versus running to the cameras. But how much good can a Congress member in 2021 actually do now if they don't take advantage of AOC's type of media exposure, if they're not doing in some ways what Eric Swalwell is doing or and being on camera a lot. Are there different strengths that workhorses have than show horses have and vice versa?",
