    "turn_text": "it changed a lot. had to change a lot, much more than any other previous edition. It's partly that 15 years have passed, but it's also that the institution has changed. And in what you've said, you've anticipated a lot of what I'm having to deal with. The institution is far more polarized, far more hyper-partisan. far more ideological in the sense of having members who, you know, are your tailor green is a extreme example, but she's not the only example of people who are just kind of out there on their own weight length. And makes it hard, makes it hard to put coalitions together, cooperative efforts together. And then it's more centralized, partly because it's more conflictful and more difficult, then you got to have stronger leadership to get things done. And then you add to that, all these crises we're dealing with. I mean, the pandemic, of course, is in a class to itself, but it's not the only crisis. I mean, we've had government shutdowns, we've had one kind of budget implosion or another for years, man-made crises, but then I guess who has to come in and pick up the pieces. It's the",
