    "turn_idx": 158,
    "turn_text": "That's not getting the bipartisan support that one would hope that it would back in the CARES Act and the other things we enacted last year, some got bipartisan support, although even them, Mitch McConnell, sat on this for a long time. It was not easy. But now with Democrats in charge, it really needs to be seen how much Republicans will feel like they want to cooperate. This is something that we're passing on a basis that gets around the Senate filibuster. When you hear people talk about doing reconciliation, that's what it means. It's a way of packaging the measure to get around the filibuster so that 50 plus one can pass it in the Senate. And that's probably true. It's probably what we need to do unless you want to mess around with this for months. and still not get many Republican votes. So it's disappointing. But there will be some Republican votes for this, I think, in the end. And then comes the other piece, the infrastructure. And here, too, there's been a lot of bipartisan talk. And everybody here says there for infrastructure. And so I'm chairman of the Appropriations Subcommittee that funds infrastructure. So I'm going to be a part of this.",
