    "turn_idx": 161,
    "turn_text": "I want to do it as cooperatively as possible. I'll just put it that way. But there again, I don't know. The economists, even some very conservative economists, tell us that this is the time to invest. This is the time to bring the economy back and to make some investments interest rates are low. We borrow now, but we will deal with some of these budget issues later. But this is the time the danger of Jerome Powell, the head of the Fed says, is not going too large. The danger is going too small. I feel that way about an infrastructure bill. It's been a long time coming. But there too, I think the chances of full bipartisan cooperation are not great. The chances of some bipartisan cooperation, I think we can manage.",
