    "turn_idx": 163,
    "turn_text": "No, no, it's a legitimate worry. But I don't think we had any choice but to hold him accountable for what he instigated and for the big lie that led up to this, where he, for the first time in American history, We really wanted to stay in power despite a free and fair election. That didn't want to transfer power and wanted a mob to storm the capital to halt the electoral count. I mean, just think about that. That's really, really over the line in terms of basic democratic practice. So I think we had to hold him accountable. I think a lot of Republicans like Liz Cheney, I think was a stand up person on this. They recognized this. That doesn't mean we We can do a number of things at the same time, and I hope we're demonstrating it this week, because this very week we're going to pass the relief bill, and we'll go on from there. Donald Trump any more than we have to, but I do think the impeachment was fully warranted just because of the egregiousness of the offense and the precedent we would have said if we let it go.",
