    "turn_text": "I don't think any of us should think our region probably is the whole ball of wax, but I love the South, and I especially love the new South. I came from a small town in East Tennessee that was really not very southern. This was a union territory during the Civil War over there in East Tennessee, and then I came into the more typical south and it's been a political battle ever since with the forces that are contending for southern allegiance. I think our region has produced its share of reactionaries and racists. I mean, we know the history. But we also know that it's hard to beat the South",
